                "EN" : "",
                "IT" : "L`Organo Woerle"
            },
            "description" : {
                "EN" : "Recently restored and redelivered to the Giovo community on 18th November 2005, this is a rare example of the organs of the Trentino area: it is the only one of its type in the province. This precious instrument presents an unequivocal union between two historic artistic styles: the Tyrolean and the Venetian. There is a small curious detail regarding the instrument: the presence of the broken octave both on the pedal and on the keyboard and a complex of registers suitable for the performance of the baroque repertoire. \nLocality: Parish Church of Assunta at Verla di Giovo",
                "IT" : "L’organo Woerle a Verla di Giovo rappresenta una rarità nel panorama del patrimonio organario trentino: è infatti il solo nel suo genere presente in provincia di Trento."
