            "name" : {
                "IT" : "ALLA LOGGIA DELL'IMPERATORE - ANGELI STEFANIA"
            },
            "description" : {
                "EN" : "\"Alla Loggia Dell´Imperatore\" is in Levico Terme, a tourist town in the popular Valsugana. It is 18 km from Trento and is easily reached by car or by train and bus. \nThe location, renowned for its arsenic-ferruginous waters, was first discovered by the Hapsburg Family who resided here during the summer season to take advantage of the therapeutic waters. Today, everyone can attain wellbeing from this natural resource in the recently renovated Spa.\n\nThe splendid Levico Lake offers a choice of private and public beaches for bathing, unforgettable leisurely walks along its shores, fishing, canoeing and lots more.\nIn the surrounding mountains above Levico, in Vetriolo, you can visit the highest altitude Spa in Europe and the Panarotta which is part of the Lagorai mountain range. In the summer months these mountains are the perfect place for hiking and gentle walks and in winter 18 km of downhill ski runs will satisfy skiers of all levels. \n\nThe Vezzena plateau also dominates Levico terme. Here cows graze in the summer mountain pastures and the local Vezzena cheese can be tasted and bought directly from the small mountain dairy farms. In winter, the scenery changes into white rolling hills where cross-country skiing and even sleddogs offer moments of fun and excitement.",
